==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*sitjaną}}, from {{m|gem-pro||*set-}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*sed-||sit}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{m|ofs|sitta}} ({{etyl|fy|-}} {{m|fy|sitte}}), {{etyl|goh|-}} {{m|goh|sizzan}}, {{m|goh|sizzen}} ({{etyl|de|-}} {{m|de|sitzen}}), {{etyl|osx|-}} {{m|osx|sittian}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{m|nl|zitten}}, {{etyl|non|-}} {{m|non|sitja}} ({{etyl|is|-}} {{m|is|sitja}}, {{etyl|fo|-}} {{m|fo|sita}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{m|sv|sitta}}), {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐍃𐌹𐍄𐌰𐌽}}. The {{etyl|ine-pro|-}} root is also the source of {{etyl|sa|-}} {{m|sa|sc=Deva|सीदति|tr=sīdati}}, {{etyl|xcl|-}} {{m|xcl|նիստ||sitting}}, {{etyl|sga|-}} {{m|sga|saidid}} ({{etyl|ga|-}} {{m|ga|suigh}}), {{etyl|grc|-}} {{m|grc|ἕζομαι}}, {{etyl|la|-}} {{m|la|sedeō}}, {{etyl|cu|-}} {{m|cu|sc=Cyrs|сѣдѣти}} ({{etyl|ru|-}} {{m|ru|сиде́ть}}).

